{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788132823,"nonce":"APjhT34OvWIXnSeM71qeSgBtJFU=","message":"AMENDMENT from the action-surface audit — orchestrator, session 4.\n\n**1. Three vanilla letter classes break the \"options by label or index\" contract.**\nThe spec's contract is \"options by label or index, exactly as 2.4 reports them\".\nThese do not have option lists in that sense:\n- `NewQuestLetter.OpenLetter` (`Verse/NewQuestLetter.cs:24-30`) switches to the\n  Quests main tab, selects the quest and removes the letter; its `Choices`\n  (`:8-22`) are only View/Jump/Close. **So a quest offer cannot be accepted from\n  the letter — which is this spec's second acceptance criterion.**\n- `ChoiceLetter_GrowthMoment.OpenLetter` (`RimWorld/ChoiceLetter_GrowthMoment.cs:125-131`)\n  opens a custom passion/trait grid (`Dialog_GrowthMomentChoices`, `forcePause` at `:66`).\n- `BundleLetter.OpenLetter` (`Verse/BundleLetter.cs:35-41`) opens a FloatMenu of\n  sub-letters.\n\n**2. Quest accept is therefore its own verb, not a letter choice.**\n`Quest.Accept(Pawn by)` (`RimWorld/Quest.cs:344`), gated by\n`QuestUtility.CanAcceptQuest` (`:268`) and per-pawn `CanPawnAcceptQuest` (`:252`);\n`RequiresAccepter` (`Quest.cs:139`). Quests with a `QuestPart_Choice` need a\nreward choice made AT accept time (`MainTabWindow_Quests.cs:613-617`).\n`dismissed` (`Quest.cs:43`) is cosmetic filtering, not a decline. **M3 needs\nthis** — Hospitality/Guests content arrives largely as quests.\n\n**3. The comms actions live in private lambdas and must be reimplemented**\n(~3 lines each). The spec's generic DiaNode walker is the right shape but will\nnot reach them:\n- request caravan trader — `RimWorld/FactionDialogMaker.cs:310-312`\n- request orbital trader — `:246-248`\n- request military aid — `CallForAid` `:500-509`\n- gift silver is NOT a comms action; it is trade gift mode,\n  `RimWorld/TradeDeal.cs:157` → `RimWorld.Planet/FactionGiftUtility.cs:29`\n- goodwill directly: `Faction.TryAffectGoodwillWith` (`RimWorld/Faction.cs:579`)\n`MainTabWindow_Factions` is **read-only** (`FactionUIUtility.cs` has only\ninfo-card popups) — do not spec a \"factions tab\" verb.\n\n**4. Trade is not instantaneous.** Both entry points require a pawn to take a\njob first: comms console `Building_CommsConsole.GiveUseCommsJob` (`:105`, plus\nthe power/EMP gate `CanUseCommsNow` at `:12`), map trader\n`FloatMenuOptionProvider_Trade.cs:56`. So `trade start` is order-then-advance-\nthen-transact, which changes the verb's shape and its rwtest assertions.\n\n**5. See the new issue 1.7 (8555381).** A timing-out letter opens ITSELF\nmid-advance and stacks a `forcePause` window, after which `LetterStack\n.OpenAutomaticLetters` early-returns forever and every subsequent timing-out\nletter silently expires. 1.7 makes `advance` halt on `dialog` rather than tick\nunderneath it; **this spec owns what to DO with the window once it is up.** The\ndivision is deliberate: 1.7 stops and reports, 3.5 decides.","files":null}]}